    "name": "fill-blanks",
    "text": "<p>If we wanted the <code>fullName</code> field to contain a <code>String</code> with a space in it, we could use <code>+</code> again:</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"450px\" scrolling=\"no\" src=\"https://tech.io/playground-widget/b6bf759a164313c4cab47a2fff43aad549685/welcome/1084067/Conctenating%20Strings\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>\n\n<p>Since a <code>String</code> consists of a sequence of characters, sometimes we might also want to consider how many characters are in a given <code>String</code>. The quotation marks are part of the way we write out <code>String</code> values, but these quotation marks are not included in the length. The length of the <code>String</code> is determined by the number of characters in between the quotes, including spaces, numbers, and punctuation. For example, <code>\"Eritrea\"</code> contains 7 characters, and <code>\"s00peR_C_kret\"</code> contains 13 characters.</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"color: #cc0000;\">Do Now! </span>Run the code above and use its output to answer the questions. </h3>",
